            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use a recurrence after a head, then add the cases in which the first head occurs before three tails.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $h$ be the probability of ending with $HH$ when the latest flip is a head and the experiment has not stopped. Here $H$ and $T$ denote heads and tails.\n\nStarting from this state, the next stopping or return cases are $H$, $TH$, $TTH$ and $TTT$. Their probabilities are $\\frac12$, $\\frac14$, $\\frac18$ and $\\frac18$. The first wins; the middle two return to the same state; the last loses.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}h&=\\frac12+\\frac14h+\\frac18h\\\\h&=\\frac12+\\frac38h\\\\\\frac58h&=\\frac12\\\\h&=\\frac45\\end{align*}$$\n\nFrom the start, the first head occurs in one of the mutually exclusive cases $H$, $TH$ or $TTH$. The remaining case, $TTT$, loses.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{ends with }HH)&=\\left(\\frac12+\\frac14+\\frac18\\right)h\\\\P(\\text{ends with }HH)&=\\frac78\\times\\frac45\\\\P(\\text{ends with }HH)&=\\frac7{10}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
